"Zeridee-und'h, called Zeridee, is Ambassador Bash-nor's Artonan assistant on Anesidora."
"She is about five feet tall, with a floor-length dark purple braid and pale brown iris rings."
"She speaks very clear English, uses human hand gestures and loves oranges."
"She is not a wizard, and tries to know every Avowed in her area."
"In the Matadero flooding she stayed at the unshielded residence to turn people away."
"Burglars stabbed her; she killed their Brute with his own stake and sent the flyer off."
"Alden preserved her and carried her, strapped on by her braid, across flooded Apex."
"She was shocked to learn Alden is friends with Stu-art'h."
"She is a daughter of the und'h family, somewhat more than twice Alden's age."
"Raised toward the wizard class, she has tried since youth to join the ordinary class instead."
"She killed all three Avowed burglars, as the Contract confirmed to Esh."
"Porti-loth healed her while she lay buried in a makeshift healing grove; she will recover."
"While healing her braid was shaved and her iris rings removed; she wears a knitted sack."
"She told Alden her attackers were not his fault, and urged him to think of Stuart and Alis."
"She is young for her post, and chose to live on Earth among Avowed for her own reasons."
"She let Alden carry her to train his skill, which works unusually thoroughly on her."
"Recovering from brain trauma, she wears a seed-stitched cap Porti-loth made."
"At the Christmas market she tried to tackle Graham, likely to protect him."
"The und'h call her their wayward daughter; custom lets Alden claim her weight in manyadeeth."
